**: Before using `global_best_position` in the `optimize` method, ensure it is initialized. You can set it to the best position of the first particle after evaluating it.\n   \n   ```python\n   def optimize(self, objective_function, iterations):\n       for _ in range(iterations):\n           for particle in self.particles:\n               particle.update_velocity(self.global_best_position)\n               particle.update_position(bounds)\n               particle.evaluate(objective_function)\n\n               # Update global best position and value\n               if particle.best_value < self.global_best_value:\n                   self.global_best_value = particle.best_value\n                   self.global_best_position = particle.position\n   ```\n\n2. **Improve Comments**: Add more detailed comments and docstrings to all methods. Explain the parameters, return values, and overall purpose of each method.\n\n3. **Consider Particle's Best Position**: In the `update_velocity` method, include the particle's own best position when updating its velocity.\n\nBy addressing these issues, the code will be more robust, user-friendly, and aligned with the task requirements."}], 'metadata': {'source': 'Code Reviewer', 'context_trace': [{'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'metadata': {'source': 'Code Reviewer'}, 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_7COZ3XoXg6DYfNkonV2IrkDd', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'describe_available_files', 'arguments': '{"recursive":true}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '{\n  "files": [\n    {\n      "id": "attachments",\n      "name": "attachments",\n      "source": "workspace",\n      "path": "attachments",\n      "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\particle-swarm-optimization_20260531155739\\\\code_workspace\\\\attachments",\n      "type": "directory",\n      "size": null,\n      "depth": 1\n    },\n    {\n      "id": "main.py",\n      "name": "main.py",\n      "source": "workspace",\n      "pa