cle.position\\n30:                if particle_value < self.global_best_value:\\n31:                    self.global_best_value = particle_value\\n32:                    self.global_best_position = particle.position\\n33:\\n34:    def update_position(self):\\n35:        \\"\\"\\"\\n36:        Update the particles\' positions based on their velocities and keep them within bounds.\\n37:        \\"\\"\\"\\n38:        for particle in self.particles:\\n39:            particle.update_position(self.bounds)\\n40:\\n",\n  "truncated": true,\n  "file_size": 2266,\n  "modified_ts": 1780235994.2153425,\n  "mode": "line_range"\n}{\n  "path": "utils.py",\n  "encoding": "utf-8-sig",\n  "newline": "\\r\\n",\n  "start_line": 1,\n  "end_line": 32,\n  "line_count": 40,\n  "lines_returned": 32,\n  "total_lines": 32,\n  "snippet": "1:\\"\\"\\"\\r\\n2:\\r\\n3:Utility functions for the PSO algorithm.\\r\\n4:\\r\\n5:\\"\\"\\"\\r\\n6:\\r\\n7:def objective_function(x):\\r\\n8:\\r\\n9:    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\n10:\\r\\n11:    Sample objective function: f(x) = x^2\\r\\n12:\\r\\n13:    This function is to be minimized.\\r\\n14:\\r\\n15:    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\n16:\\r\\n17:\\"\\"\\"\\r\\n18:\\r\\n19:\\r\\n20:\\r\\n21:def objective_function(x):\\r\\n22:\\r\\n23:    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\n24:\\r\\n25:    Sample objective function: f(x) = x^2\\r\\n26:\\r\\n27:    This function is to be minimized.\\r\\n28:\\r\\n29:    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\n30:\\r\\n31:    return sum([xi ** 2 for xi in x])\\r\\n32:\\r\\n",\n  "truncated": false,\n  "file_size": 373,\n  "modified_ts": 1780235941.2382276,\n  "mode": "line_range"\n}', 'output': "Upon reviewing the provided source codes, I have identified several areas that need attention to ensure compliance with the specified regulations and to enhance the overall functionality of the PSO algorithm implementation.\n\n### Comments with Priority\n\n1. **Duplicate Definition of `objective_function`:** In `utils.py`, the `objective_function` is defined twice, which would lead to confusion and potential