all Dependencies**: Install the required packages using pip. Run the following command:\n   ```bash\n   pip install numpy matplotlib\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the PSO Implementation\n1. **Import the PSO Module**: Import the PSO class from the module in your Python script.\n   ```python\n   from pso_module import PSO\n   ```\n\n2. **Define the Objective Function**: Create a function that defines the optimization problem you want to solve. For example:\n   ```python\n   def objective_function(x):\n       return x**2  # Simple function to minimize\n   ```\n\n3. **Initialize PSO**: Create an instance of the PSO class with the desired parameters.\n   ```python\n   pso = PSO(objective_function, population_size=30, max_iterations=100)\n   ```\n\n4. **Run the Algorithm**: Call the run method to start the optimization process.\n   ```python\n   best_position, best_fitness = pso.run()\n   print(f'Best Position: {best_position}, Best Fitness: {best_fitness}')\n   ```\n\n5. **Visualize Results** (Optional): You can use matplotlib to visualize the optimization process, if implemented in the module.\n\n## Conclusion\nThis PSO implementation is designed to be simple and effective, allowing users to easily adapt it for their optimization problems. For further details on specific functions and parameters, please refer to the source code documentation.\n\n---\n\nFor any issues or feature requests, feel free to reach out to the development team.", 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
