 'create_folder', 'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'metadata': {'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}, 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_0Mqf7w1FAdkAbdKfzeANkj7l', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'save_file', 'arguments': '{"path":"manuals/manual.md","content":"# User Manual for Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) Algorithm Implementation\\n\\n## Introduction\\nThe Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) algorithm is a popular optimization technique inspired by social behavior patterns of birds and fish. This implementation aims to provide an easy-to-understand and user-friendly way to apply PSO to various optimization problems.\\n\\n## Main Functions\\n1. **Initialization**: Set up the parameters for the PSO algorithm, including population size, number of iterations, and bounds for the search space.\\n2. **Update Velocity and Position**: Update the velocity and position of particles based on their own best-known position and the best-known position of the swarm.\\n3. **Fitness Evaluation**: Evaluate the fitness of each particle based on the defined objective function.\\n4. **Convergence Check**: Check whether the algorithm has converged based on specified criteria.\\n5. **Result Retrieval**: Retrieve the best-found solution and the corresponding fitness value.\\n\\n## Installation Instructions\\nTo run the PSO algorithm implementation, you need to set up your Python environment with the required dependencies. Follow the steps below:\\n\\n1. **Install Python**: Ensure that you have Python installed on your system. You can download it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\\n\\n2. **Create a Virtual Environment** (optional but recommended):  \\n   Open your terminal or command prompt and run:\\n   ```bash\\n   python -m venv pso-env\\n   ```\\n   Activate the virtual environment:\\n   - On Windows:  \\n     ```bash\\n     .\\\\pso-env\\\\Scripts\\\\activate\\n     ```  \\n   - On macOS/Linux:  \\n     ```bash\\n     source pso-env/bin/activate\\n     ```\\n\\n3. **Install Dependencies**: Install the required packages using pip. Run the following command:\\n   ```bash\\n   pip install numpy matplotlib\\n   ```\\n\\n## How to Use the PSO Implementation\\n1. **Import the PSO Module**: Import the PSO class from the module in your Python script.\\n   ```python\\n   from pso_module import PSO\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Define the Objective Function**: Create a function that defines the optimization problem you want to solve. For example:\\n   ```python\\n   def objective_function(x):\\n       return x**2  # Simple function to minimize\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Initialize PSO**: Create an instance of the PSO class with the desired parameters.\\n   ```python\\n   pso = PSO(objective_function, population_size=30, max_iterations=100)\\n   ```\\n\\n4. **Run the Algorithm**: Call the run method to start the optimization process.\\n   ```python\\n   best_position, best_fitness = pso.run()\\n   print(f\'Best Position: {best_position}, Best Fitness: {best_fitness}\')\\n   ```\\n\\n5. **Visualize Results** (Optional): You can use matplotlib to visualize the optimization process, if implemented in the module.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nThis PSO implementation is designed to be simple and effective, allowing users to easily adapt it for their optimization problems. For further details on specific functions and parameters, please refer to the source code documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFor any issues or feature requests, feel free to reach out to the development team.","encoding":"utf-8","mode":"overwrite"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '{\n  "path": "manuals/manual.md",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\particle-swarm-optimization_20260531155739\\\\code_workspace\\\\manuals\\\\manual.md",\n  "size": 3088\n}', 'tool_call_id': 'call_0Mqf7w1FAdkAbdKfzeANkj7l', 'metadata': {'tool_name': 'save_file', 'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content'